zU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-07T13:47:10Z","updated_at":"2025-04-07T13:50:47Z","body":"Correct, Godot's YXZ is order is intrinsically Y then X then Z when composing, or extrinsically Z then X then Y when composing, or intrinsically Z then X then Y when decomposing, or extrinsically Y then X then Z when decomposing. This is all quite a mouthful, and I'm not sure what's the most concise way to convey this information. I think when people see YXZ they assume intrinsic+composing, but somehow this should be explicitly documented.\n\n> blender is implicitly referring to an extrinsic order\n\nThat explains why I always found Euler angles in Blender infuriatingly difficult to use! 😛 ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2783404846/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2783416771","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105115#issuecomment-2783416771","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105115","id":2783416771,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6l55HD","user":{"login":"FreyaHolmer","id":3438510,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0Mzg1MTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3438510?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FreyaHolmer","html_url":"https://github.com/FreyaHolmer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FreyaHolmer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FreyaHolmer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FreyaHolmer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FreyaHolmer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FreyaHolmer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FreyaHolmer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FreyaHolmer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FreyaHolmer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FreyaHolmer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-07T13:50:46Z","updated_at":"2025-04-07T13:50:46Z","body":"I think the most low hanging fruit would be to plop it into a tooltip on the rotation order field. Another would be to use the x-y'-z\" notation in the UI, although it might be a good idea to only use that notation in the dropdown menu when unfolded, to avoid cluttering the UI, or at least use lowercase letters to make it at a bare minimum distinct from wikipedia's and blender's use of uppercase for the extrinsic order","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2783416771/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2784916531","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105115#issuecomment-2784916531","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105115","id":2784916531,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6l_nQz","user":{"login":"Rindbee","id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-08T00:21:17Z","updated_at":"2025-04-08T00:33:51Z","body":"It is recommended to use +/- signs to represent extrinsic/intrinsic order respectively. Currently it is common to use uppercase and lowercase letters for distinction, although this may be ignored in formatted displays.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2784916531/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2875972052","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105115#issuecomment-2875972052","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105115"